Subject: yq2.cfg: W/A/S/D and a game controller's buttons by default

Walnut is a console. Yamagi's defaults moved with E/S/D/F (A and G
turning), and bound none of a game controller's buttons, so a pad
could move and look (the sticks are the engine's own) but not fire.

- W/A/S/D move and strafe; the power shield moves from W to E.
- A game controller by place: R2 fires, L2 walks, Cross jumps, Circle
  crouches, L1/R1 the previous/next weapon, Square uses the selected
  item, Triangle the inventory, D-pad left/right selects an item, up the
  help computer, down drops the item, Select the score. Start is the
  menu already.

yq2.cfg runs right after default.cfg and before the player's
config.cfg, so these are defaults: a saved configuration keeps its own
bindings, and the menu's "reset to defaults" gives these.

Forwarded: not-needed

diff --git a/stuff/yq2.cfg b/stuff/yq2.cfg
--- a/stuff/yq2.cfg
+++ b/stuff/yq2.cfg
@@ -29,12 +29,11 @@ bind	0		"use BFG10K"
 
 bind	MOUSE1		+attack
 
-bind	d		+back
-bind	e		+forward
-bind	s		+moveleft
-bind	a		+left
-bind	f		+moveright
-bind	g		+right
+// Walnut: W/A/S/D as most players know them (Yamagi's E/S/D/F, with A and G turning, before)
+bind	w		+forward
+bind	s		+back
+bind	a		+moveleft
+bind	d		+moveright
 
 bind	TAB		inven
 bind	ENTER		invuse
@@ -46,7 +45,7 @@ bind	MWHEELDOWN	weapprev
 bind	MWHEELUP	weapnext
 
 bind	q		"use quad damage"
-bind	w		"use power shield"
+bind	e		"use power shield"
 
 bind	SHIFT		+speed
 
@@ -62,6 +61,25 @@ bind	F12		screenshot jpg 90
 
 bind	t		messagemode
 
+// Walnut: a game controller (a DualShock) plays as it comes. The left stick moves, the right
+// stick looks (the engine's own), Start is the menu (built in); the buttons by their place:
+// R2 fires, L2 walks, Cross jumps, Circle crouches, L1/R1 the previous/next weapon, Square uses the
+// selected item, Triangle the inventory, the D-pad left/right selects an item, D-pad up the
+// help computer, D-pad down drops the item, Select the score.
+bind	TRIG_RIGHT	+attack
+bind	TRIG_LEFT	+speed
+bind	BTN_SOUTH	+moveup
+bind	BTN_EAST	+movedown
+bind	SHOULDR_LEFT	weapprev
+bind	SHOULDR_RIGHT	weapnext
+bind	BTN_WEST	invuse
+bind	BTN_NORTH	inven
+bind	DP_LEFT		invprev
+bind	DP_RIGHT	invnext
+bind	DP_UP		"cmd help"
+bind	DP_DOWN		invdrop
+bind	BTN_BACK	"cmd score"
+
 //----------------------------------------------
 
